sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch03-21> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Van’t Hoff’s law, that reaction velocity is multiplied by a constant factor for each degree of temperature rise, applies with qualifications to growth, so that growth has a temperature coefficient (about 2 to 3 per 10 °C, of the same order as chemical reactions).";
    dc:type "mathematical-law";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Growth has a van’t Hoff temperature coefficient like a chemical reaction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "v(\\theta + n) = x^n v(\\theta) for a rise of n degrees; temperature coefficient of growth x^{10} \\approx 2\\text{--}3";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter III, “The Rate of Growth”; topic “Effect of temperature”. Scope: growth and development of plants and animals within normal temperature limits"
}
